{"content":"Found the bug: in group_as's valid_next (sqlparse/engine/grouping.py), the check order is `not imt(token, t=ttypes) and token is not None`. Since Python evaluates left-to-right, `imt(token, ...)` gets called even when `token` is None (i.e., there's no token after AS), and `imt` does `token.ttype in t`, raising `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'ttype'`. This differs from every other `valid_next`/`valid_prev` helper in the file, which check `token is not None` first. I'll swap the order and then run the test suite to confirm the fix.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/engine/grouping.py","old_text":"    def valid_next(token):
        ttypes = T.DML, T.DDL, T.CTE
        return not imt(token, t=ttypes) and token is not None","new_text":"    def valid_next(token):
        ttypes = T.DML, T.DDL, T.CTE
        return token is not None and not imt(token, t=ttypes)"}},{"id":"call_2","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -m pytest tests -q","timeout_seconds":120}}]}

arguments.old_text:
def valid_next(token):
    ttypes = T.DML, T.DDL, T.CTE
